1
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:08,033
(Overnight Stay Application)
"Shiono".

2
00:00:08,133 --> 00:00:11,033
Shiono? You mean that Shiono?

3
00:00:12,133 --> 00:00:14,133
Yeah, that's right.

4
00:00:16,267 --> 00:00:19,200
Are you two close enough
to go on a trip together?

5
00:00:20,033 --> 00:00:23,567
They're in the same club.

6
00:00:24,167 --> 00:00:25,067
A club?

7
00:00:25,167 --> 00:00:26,333
Yeah.

8
00:00:26,433 --> 00:00:30,400
The Yama-no-michi Police
Station Hot Spring Club.

9
00:00:31,167 --> 00:00:32,233
There's a club for that?

10
00:00:32,333 --> 00:00:32,967
Yep.

11
00:00:33,067 --> 00:00:34,533
It was just formed recently.

12
00:00:34,633 --> 00:00:36,100
A hot spring club.

13
00:00:36,567 --> 00:00:39,033
So we figured Takoi and
Shiono could go check things out.

14
00:00:39,133 --> 00:00:40,167
I see.

15
00:00:40,633 --> 00:00:42,433
Maybe I should join too.

16
00:00:42,533 --> 00:00:46,033
Oh! But we're not taking
new members right now.

17
00:00:46,133 --> 00:00:48,200
- It's really popular.
- That's right.

18
00:00:48,933 --> 00:00:50,900
You just got here, after all.

19
00:00:51,067 --> 00:00:52,307
We're already at full capacity.

20
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:53,633
I'll be going now.

21
00:00:54,133 --> 00:00:55,533
I didn't realize it was so popular.

22
00:00:56,133 --> 00:00:57,200
Sorry about that.

23
00:00:58,033 --> 00:00:59,700
Excuse me.

24
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:00,867
- Good work.
- Yeah.

25
00:01:04,533 --> 00:01:05,633
Thanks.

26
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:08,300
Yeah.

27
00:01:08,933 --> 00:01:11,500
You don't really need to worry about it.

28
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:12,600
Huh?

29
00:01:13,233 --> 00:01:14,433
It's fine, isn't it?

30
00:01:15,067 --> 00:01:16,900
Even if it's just you and Shiono going.

31
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:19,600
You guys are a couple anyway.

32
00:01:19,767 --> 00:01:21,033
Exactly.

33
00:01:21,333 --> 00:01:23,167
There's no need to hide it from everyone.

34
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:26,000
Have a great time.

35
00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:28,433
- Bring back some good food!
- Yay!

36
00:01:29,667 --> 00:01:30,867
Will do.

37
00:01:57,767 --> 00:02:01,100
"Duty First, Kiss Later"

38
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:04,733
(Episode 9)

39
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:07,800
Wow! This view is amazing!

40
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:09,267
It really is nice.

41
00:02:09,367 --> 00:02:10,533
Incredible.

42
00:02:10,900 --> 00:02:11,700
Look.

43
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:12,867
Odawara Castle.

44
00:02:12,967 --> 00:02:15,467
I heard it's known as
the "impregnable castle."

45
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:18,667
You actually looked that up?

46
00:02:19,233 --> 00:02:20,367
Something like that.

47
00:02:21,733 --> 00:02:22,500
Excuse me.

48
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,433
- Yes?
- Could you take a picture for us?

49
00:02:24,533 --> 00:02:25,700
Sure thing.

50
00:02:25,933 --> 00:02:27,833
Alright, say cheese.

51
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:29,933
- Thank you.
- Thanks.

52
00:02:30,033 --> 00:02:31,033
No problem.

53
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:33,933
Would you like me to take one of you two?

54
00:02:34,333 --> 00:02:36,200
Oh, no need.

55
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:37,867
Let's do it.

56
00:02:39,033 --> 00:02:40,100
Okay.

57
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:41,700
We'd appreciate it.

58
00:02:42,333 --> 00:02:43,867
Alright, here we go.

59
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:46,233
Smile, smile.

60
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:49,567
Okay, looking good.

61
00:02:50,333 --> 00:02:51,500
Great, great.

62
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:52,000
Here you go.

63
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:53,200
Oh, thank you.

64
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:54,309
- Thanks.
- You're welcome.

65
00:02:54,333 --> 00:02:56,933
- Thank you.
- Thanks.

66
00:03:02,100 --> 00:03:05,367
Oh, it's Ninomiya Kinjiro.

67
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:09,533
Ninomiya Kinjiro was born
in Kayama Village, Odawara.

68
00:03:09,633 --> 00:03:11,067
Wow, you know a lot.

69
00:03:13,333 --> 00:03:15,300
- It says so right here.
- Oh, it's written there.

70
00:03:16,767 --> 00:03:18,200
It really does.

71
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:19,733
Born in Kayama Village, Odawara.

72
00:03:19,833 --> 00:03:21,467
Oh.

73
00:03:22,267 --> 00:03:23,367
- Let's eat.
- Let's eat.

74
00:03:23,467 --> 00:03:25,500
Here you go, enjoy.

75
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:29,400
- Mmm, this is delicious.
- It really is.

76
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:31,167
Thank you.

77
00:03:31,267 --> 00:03:31,667
Mmm.

78
00:03:31,767 --> 00:03:32,967
Could I have another one?

79
00:03:33,067 --> 00:03:34,300
Sure, here you go.

80
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:35,476
You're eating way too much.

81
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:36,500
But it's so good.

82
00:03:37,033 --> 00:03:39,633
Can I have one too?

83
00:03:41,967 --> 00:03:42,667
Thanks.

84
00:03:42,767 --> 00:03:43,967
No problem.

85
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:47,600
Thank you.

86
00:03:48,867 --> 00:03:50,067
Ah.

87
00:03:50,167 --> 00:03:51,367
Huh?

88
00:03:51,473 --> 00:03:54,206
No, no, this is too...

89
00:03:54,300 --> 00:03:55,533
It's fine.

90
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:58,967
It's rare for us to be here
together, let's just enjoy it.

91
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:01,600
Here.

92
00:04:07,367 --> 00:04:08,367
Delicious!

93
00:04:12,700 --> 00:04:13,967
Mmm! So good!

94
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:15,233
Yummy!

95
00:04:15,767 --> 00:04:17,233
Here, have some of this too.

96
00:04:17,333 --> 00:04:18,333
Okay.

97
00:04:21,133 --> 00:04:22,733
Mmm.

98
00:04:23,433 --> 00:04:24,833
This is really good too.

99
00:04:26,700 --> 00:04:27,867
Yeah, it's delicious.

100
00:04:28,267 --> 00:04:29,267
Right?

101
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:30,433
Yeah.

102
00:04:30,533 --> 00:04:32,400
Can we buy souvenirs over there?

103
00:04:33,567 --> 00:04:35,100
We can just buy them on the way back.

104
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:37,700
We still need to get something
for Egawa and the others.

105
00:04:38,567 --> 00:04:39,967
Let's just get food.

106
00:04:40,433 --> 00:04:43,233
Yeah, they'll probably
like whatever we get.

107
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:45,433
I think so too.

108
00:04:48,300 --> 00:04:49,900
Wow!

109
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,767
This place is really nice.

110
00:04:51,867 --> 00:04:53,533
- It really is.
- Yeah.

111
00:04:54,067 --> 00:04:55,400
Should we open the window?

112
00:05:01,100 --> 00:05:04,667
Hot springs, food,
drink. This is the life.

113
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:07,233
Looks like we'll be dining in the room.

114
00:05:07,333 --> 00:05:08,667
I wonder if they have sashimi.

115
00:05:08,767 --> 00:05:10,633
Oh, I wonder if they have kamaboko.

116
00:05:11,433 --> 00:05:12,673
I heard the oden here is great.

117
00:05:12,733 --> 00:05:13,809
The person at the front
desk recommended it.

118
00:05:13,833 --> 00:05:15,133
Oh, oden.

119
00:05:16,867 --> 00:05:17,867
Oh!

120
00:05:22,267 --> 00:05:23,933
Not bad.

121
00:05:24,033 --> 00:05:26,167
When it comes to hot
springs, you gotta wear this.

122
00:05:27,067 --> 00:05:28,333
Let's put them on later.

123
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:33,867
What?

124
00:05:36,867 --> 00:05:38,667
Just seeing that look on your face...

125
00:05:38,767 --> 00:05:40,200
Makes this whole trip worth it.

126
00:05:43,233 --> 00:05:44,533
Oh.

127
00:05:45,133 --> 00:05:46,333
Let's enjoy ourselves.

128
00:05:47,067 --> 00:05:48,133
Yeah.

129
00:05:50,633 --> 00:05:51,200
Hey.

130
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:52,300
This is yours.

131
00:05:52,367 --> 00:05:53,667
Thanks.

132
00:05:54,533 --> 00:05:56,500
Ah, this feels amazing.

133
00:05:56,900 --> 00:05:57,767
It really does.

134
00:05:57,867 --> 00:05:59,833
Hot springs are definitely the best.

135
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:01,100
Yeah.

136
00:06:01,967 --> 00:06:04,127
Wanna see who can hold
their breath underwater longer?

137
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:05,600
Huh?

138
00:06:05,700 --> 00:06:06,500
Are you serious?

139
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:07,833
I'm just kidding.

140
00:06:07,933 --> 00:06:10,367
We can't do that in a public place.

141
00:06:10,733 --> 00:06:14,167
And you're a cop, saying stuff like that.

142
00:06:16,033 --> 00:06:21,133
Speaking of cops, your first
love was a cop too, right?

143
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:22,567
Huh?

144
00:06:22,667 --> 00:06:23,667
Did I ever mention that?

145
00:06:23,767 --> 00:06:24,967
George told me.

146
00:06:25,067 --> 00:06:26,233
Oh.

147
00:06:28,033 --> 00:06:29,133
Yeah.

148
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:35,900
My first love was a handsome,
righteous police officer.

149
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:38,933
Is that so?

150
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:41,700
Take this!

151
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:42,867
Ah, sorry.

152
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:50,700
You...

153
00:06:53,667 --> 00:06:54,700
What?

154
00:06:54,933 --> 00:06:58,867
Nothing, I just really
like that face of yours.

155
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,100
Stop messing around.

156
00:07:05,667 --> 00:07:07,633
Using such childish tricks again.

157
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:12,067
- Let's eat.
- Let's eat.

158
00:07:15,033 --> 00:07:16,233
Delicious!

159
00:07:16,333 --> 00:07:17,800
Mmm, so good.

160
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:20,267
Try this, it's really good.

161
00:07:20,733 --> 00:07:22,267
I want to eat at my own pace.

162
00:07:22,367 --> 00:07:23,767
Come on, just eat it.

163
00:07:24,967 --> 00:07:26,167
You're so annoying.

164
00:07:30,067 --> 00:07:31,533
Mmm, delicious.

165
00:07:31,633 --> 00:07:33,000
Right?!

166
00:07:35,233 --> 00:07:37,967
Yeah, it's good.

167
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:39,967
This is good too.

168
00:07:40,067 --> 00:07:41,433
This goes great with beer.

169
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:50,467
Hot springs, food, drinks, and sleep.

170
00:07:50,567 --> 00:07:52,767
Ah, this is pure bliss.

171
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:56,867
Are you feeling relaxed?

172
00:07:57,100 --> 00:07:58,533
Absolutely.

173
00:07:58,633 --> 00:07:59,333
What about you?

174
00:07:59,433 --> 00:08:00,800
Yeah, very relaxed.

175
00:08:00,900 --> 00:08:01,900
Mmm.

176
00:08:04,500 --> 00:08:06,533
You don't have to worry
about anyone else here.

177
00:08:06,633 --> 00:08:09,100
You can just kick back and relax.

178
00:08:13,267 --> 00:08:14,600
Speaking of which...

179
00:08:17,900 --> 00:08:21,600
I was thinking, about us...

180
00:08:21,700 --> 00:08:23,233
Maybe we don't need to worry so much.

181
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:30,233
What's there to worry
about when dating you?

182
00:08:30,333 --> 00:08:32,043
When I submitted the
overnight stay application...

183
00:08:32,067 --> 00:08:33,867
I did wonder what to do.

184
00:08:36,367 --> 00:08:38,500
But maybe I was just overthinking it.

185
00:08:38,800 --> 00:08:41,533
Nobody else really cares that much.

186
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:43,767
Yeah.

187
00:08:45,667 --> 00:08:47,500
There's no need to
go out of our way to lie.

188
00:08:48,233 --> 00:08:51,900
Well, I never cared from the start.

189
00:09:03,333 --> 00:09:05,867
I couldn't care less
what other people think.

190
00:09:07,867 --> 00:09:11,633
But I figured it's better
to follow your lead on this.

191
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:16,867
But if we get caught lying...

192
00:09:16,967 --> 00:09:19,633
And it ruins my chances of
getting to HQ, I'd be pretty pissed.

193
00:09:19,733 --> 00:09:21,267
Huh? HQ?

194
00:09:22,033 --> 00:09:23,400
You want to go to HQ?

195
00:09:24,867 --> 00:09:26,100
You could say that.

196
00:09:26,833 --> 00:09:28,273
This is the first I'm hearing of it.

197
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:29,533
It's just a hope.

198
00:09:29,633 --> 00:09:30,867
Just a hope.

199
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:34,200
I want to work on a big case someday too.

200
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:36,533
Hmm, I had no idea.

201
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:43,033
In ten years, you'll definitely
be a superintendent.

202
00:09:43,733 --> 00:09:46,633
By then, I'll look so lame next to you.
It'd be embarrassing.

203
00:09:49,100 --> 00:09:50,100
Ten years?

204
00:09:50,733 --> 00:09:52,433
Maybe even sooner.

205
00:09:52,533 --> 00:09:54,467
I just figured it'd take about ten years.

206
00:09:56,167 --> 00:09:58,700
You've really thought that far ahead.

207
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:00,367
Huh?

208
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:04,967
That sounds a lot like a proposal.

209
00:10:05,433 --> 00:10:06,233
What?

210
00:10:06,333 --> 00:10:07,600
How is that a proposal?

211
00:10:07,967 --> 00:10:09,167
Isn't it?

212
00:10:09,833 --> 00:10:11,800
That... That's totally different.

213
00:10:12,167 --> 00:10:14,367
A proposal should be way more formal.

214
00:10:16,033 --> 00:10:19,000
So you are going to propose formally.

215
00:10:23,267 --> 00:10:24,700
I'll look forward to it then.

216
00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:31,067
Yeah.

217
00:10:50,160 --> 00:10:52,926
Your first love was also a cop, right?

218
00:10:57,733 --> 00:11:01,433
Everyone keeps asking if I like someone.

219
00:11:01,526 --> 00:11:03,226
Or if I have a girlfriend.

220
00:11:03,833 --> 00:11:05,333
It's so annoying.

221
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,143
Hey! Don't do anything stupid!

222
00:11:09,167 --> 00:11:10,167
Huh?

223
00:11:12,767 --> 00:11:13,767
Calm down!

224
00:11:13,967 --> 00:11:15,967
Jumping won't solve anything, right?

225
00:11:16,067 --> 00:11:17,167
What?

226
00:11:17,767 --> 00:11:19,967
No, I'd never do something like that.

227
00:11:20,067 --> 00:11:21,167
Huh?

228
00:11:21,267 --> 00:11:22,267
Really?

229
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:26,567
Sorry, I totally just tackled you.

230
00:11:26,667 --> 00:11:27,900
Are you okay?

231
00:11:29,033 --> 00:11:30,873
I work at the police
station right over there.

232
00:11:30,967 --> 00:11:33,067
I don't usually have anyone to talk to.

233
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:37,500
If you have anything you can't
tell others, come find me anytime.

234
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:38,633
Okay?

235
00:12:04,167 --> 00:12:06,267
- Let's eat.
- Let's eat.

236
00:12:06,767 --> 00:12:08,800
So, how was the hot spring?

237
00:12:08,900 --> 00:12:10,500
It was amazing.

238
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:11,900
The inn was fantastic too.

239
00:12:12,533 --> 00:12:14,200
I'm so jealous.

240
00:12:14,367 --> 00:12:15,600
Welcome back.

241
00:12:15,767 --> 00:12:16,833
Oh.

242
00:12:16,933 --> 00:12:18,076
Omaeda, you should have one too.

243
00:12:18,100 --> 00:12:19,000
- Can I?
- Yeah.

244
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:20,300
Don't mind if I do.

245
00:12:20,867 --> 00:12:22,900
Shiono seemed to have a blast too.

246
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,733
He soaked in the hot spring several times.

247
00:12:25,633 --> 00:12:26,533
Good work.

248
00:12:26,633 --> 00:12:27,633
Oh, good work.

249
00:12:27,667 --> 00:12:28,500
Takoi brought back souvenirs.

250
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:29,900
Here.

251
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,100
Thanks.

252
00:12:32,033 --> 00:12:33,133
Delicious.

253
00:12:33,233 --> 00:12:33,500
Really good.

254
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:35,933
I couldn't tell that guy liked hot springs.

255
00:12:36,033 --> 00:12:39,500
Then at night, I asked if he
wanted to go on a test of courage.

256
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:41,367
Turns out Shiono was scared to death.

257
00:12:42,267 --> 00:12:45,000
It was a rare trip, so I
felt a bit bad for him.

258
00:12:45,567 --> 00:12:46,433
Do you have any photos?

259
00:12:46,533 --> 00:12:47,333
Yeah.

260
00:12:47,433 --> 00:12:48,933
I do have some.

261
00:12:49,033 --> 00:12:50,433
Let me see, let me see.

262
00:12:50,900 --> 00:12:51,500
I really want to see.

263
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:54,233
- You're dying to show us, aren't you?
- Hurry up.

264
00:12:54,567 --> 00:12:55,733
How about this one?

265
00:13:00,767 --> 00:13:02,100
This one is really nice.

266
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:03,100
You guys look great together.

267
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:03,833
Stop that.

268
00:13:03,933 --> 00:13:06,333
Shiono is even smiling a little.

269
00:13:06,433 --> 00:13:07,200
- He really is.
- That's rare.

270
00:13:07,300 --> 00:13:08,167
Indeed.

271
00:13:08,267 --> 00:13:11,167
Male bonding really is something else.

272
00:13:13,067 --> 00:13:14,433
I'll grab another one then.

273
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:18,933
What, you want one too?

274
00:13:19,133 --> 00:13:19,467
Yeah.

275
00:13:19,567 --> 00:13:22,433
Can you send me that photo?

276
00:13:22,667 --> 00:13:23,367
I guess I can.

277
00:13:23,467 --> 00:13:24,467
Thanks.

278
00:13:24,500 --> 00:13:27,933
So you two made some great memories?

279
00:13:28,333 --> 00:13:29,467
Yeah.

280
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,300
You're making me blush.

281
00:13:32,400 --> 00:13:34,533
- So annoying.
- Right?

282
00:13:34,633 --> 00:13:35,400
So annoying.

283
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:38,000
Maybe I should go on a trip
with my academy buddies too.

284
00:13:40,433 --> 00:13:41,267
What do you say, want to join?

285
00:13:41,367 --> 00:13:42,467
No thanks.

286
00:13:42,900 --> 00:13:44,700
- Mind if I take this?
- Go ahead.

287
00:13:44,933 --> 00:13:45,800
How many boxes of these are left?

288
00:13:45,900 --> 00:13:47,000
Just one more.

289
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:49,100
- Don't mind if I do.
- Alright, stop taking them.

290
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:51,643
- That's his.
- Didn't your wife tell you to watch your weight?

291
00:13:51,667 --> 00:13:53,300
I'm taking it back for my wife.

292
00:13:54,033 --> 00:13:55,200
Oh, Shu.

293
00:13:55,300 --> 00:13:56,033
You're back.

294
00:13:56,133 --> 00:13:57,333
Sorry to keep you waiting.

295
00:13:58,367 --> 00:13:59,367
Here, a souvenir.

296
00:13:59,400 --> 00:14:01,967
- Wow, awesome.
- Thanks.

297
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:03,800
One oolong tea, please.

298
00:14:03,900 --> 00:14:04,300
Sure.

299
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:06,900
- Oh.
- Hot spring buns.

300
00:14:07,967 --> 00:14:09,207
The inn was pretty nice, right?

301
00:14:09,233 --> 00:14:10,433
Yeah.

302
00:14:10,533 --> 00:14:12,867
The food was delicious,
and the hot spring was great.

303
00:14:12,967 --> 00:14:13,867
Oh~.

304
00:14:13,967 --> 00:14:15,667
- Want to go on our next day off?
- Yeah.

305
00:14:15,767 --> 00:14:17,700
If Shu is free, you should come too.

306
00:14:18,067 --> 00:14:19,733
- I'll pass.
- What a shame!

307
00:14:19,833 --> 00:14:21,333
- Thanks.
- Here you go.

308
00:14:21,433 --> 00:14:22,567
Thanks.

309
00:14:23,667 --> 00:14:24,900
Let's eat.

310
00:14:25,267 --> 00:14:26,300
Hey.

311
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:27,833
Takoi is pretty popular, isn't he?

312
00:14:27,933 --> 00:14:29,033
And he's good-looking.

313
00:14:29,133 --> 00:14:30,167
True.

314
00:14:30,267 --> 00:14:32,467
I guess he's somewhat handsome.

315
00:14:32,567 --> 00:14:34,133
What do you mean "somewhat"?

316
00:14:34,233 --> 00:14:38,000
If you're not careful, someone
might snatch him away.

317
00:14:38,100 --> 00:14:39,333
Who?

318
00:14:40,633 --> 00:14:41,267
Uh.

319
00:14:41,367 --> 00:14:43,167
No one in particular.

320
00:14:43,267 --> 00:14:44,843
With a face like that and
being so nice to everyone...

321
00:14:44,867 --> 00:14:46,067
Yeah.

322
00:14:48,367 --> 00:14:51,867
Isn't Takoi your first love?

323
00:14:57,433 --> 00:14:58,600
I guess so.

324
00:14:59,667 --> 00:15:01,133
Don't let him get away.

325
00:15:02,567 --> 00:15:03,833
I know.

326
00:15:04,567 --> 00:15:06,200
- Mmm~
- Mmm~.

327
00:15:07,300 --> 00:15:09,167
- Just kidding.
- Bring it on.

328
00:15:14,333 --> 00:15:15,533
Huh?

329
00:15:20,733 --> 00:15:22,500
Oh, this.

330
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:24,267
Can't see the face.

331
00:15:25,533 --> 00:15:28,700
But we can confirm this
guy comes and goes a lot.

332
00:15:29,967 --> 00:15:32,500
I really want to search the place ASAP.

333
00:15:37,033 --> 00:15:38,667
Takoyaki maker, check.

334
00:15:38,767 --> 00:15:39,967
Octopus, check. Batter, check.

335
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,900
Skewers, check.

336
00:15:42,567 --> 00:15:43,667
Alright...

337
00:15:44,367 --> 00:15:45,900
Yeah.

338
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:48,967
It's been a while.

339
00:15:49,067 --> 00:15:50,400
Kamekichi.

340
00:15:51,500 --> 00:15:52,967
Ah, got anything to drink?

341
00:15:53,533 --> 00:15:55,633
Tea, tea.

342
00:16:00,967 --> 00:16:02,600
Hey, Shiono.

343
00:16:03,167 --> 00:16:04,067
Sorry.

344
00:16:04,167 --> 00:16:06,567
Work might run a bit late today.

345
00:16:06,833 --> 00:16:07,967
Huh?

346
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:11,967
Oh, I see.

347
00:16:12,900 --> 00:16:16,100
You're not already prepping, are you?

348
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:17,933
No.

349
00:16:21,700 --> 00:16:22,433
Sorry.

350
00:16:22,533 --> 00:16:25,667
I didn't even know what
to prep for takoyaki anyway.

351
00:16:25,767 --> 00:16:27,567
So I haven't done anything yet.

352
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:30,633
That's good.

353
00:16:30,733 --> 00:16:31,833
Yeah.

354
00:16:32,433 --> 00:16:34,433
Tomorrow works for me.

355
00:16:35,133 --> 00:16:36,133
Yeah.

356
00:16:37,733 --> 00:16:39,800
Then see you tomorrow at the usual place.

357
00:16:40,133 --> 00:16:41,467
Good luck with work.

358
00:16:41,567 --> 00:16:43,033
Make sure you eat properly, and...

359
00:16:43,133 --> 00:16:45,533
Shiono, got a minute?

360
00:16:45,633 --> 00:16:47,200
Sure, I'll be right there.

361
00:16:48,100 --> 00:16:50,867
I'm looking forward to tomorrow then.

362
00:16:51,933 --> 00:16:52,933
Yeah.

363
00:17:05,567 --> 00:17:07,300
It's work, after all.

364
00:17:07,700 --> 00:17:09,133
Can't be helped, right?

365
00:17:19,067 --> 00:17:20,867
He'll come, right?

366
00:17:21,767 --> 00:17:23,367
It's been a while since I last saw him.

367
00:17:25,967 --> 00:17:26,767
Here, on the house.

368
00:17:26,867 --> 00:17:27,933
Huh?

369
00:17:28,033 --> 00:17:30,033
The boss is feeling generous today.

370
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:36,533
Oh, welcome.

371
00:17:36,633 --> 00:17:38,400
You made it, Shiono?

372
00:17:44,033 --> 00:17:45,367
Sorry to keep you waiting...

373
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:49,100
Shiono, it's been a while.

374
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:52,133
It's been a while.

375
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:54,200
Come on, have a seat.

376
00:17:54,267 --> 00:17:55,367
Yeah.

377
00:17:55,733 --> 00:17:56,500
Okay.

378
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:57,633
Sorry.

379
00:17:57,733 --> 00:17:58,767
You're too slow.

380
00:17:58,867 --> 00:18:00,700
It's not that late.

381
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:02,100
Good work today.

382
00:18:03,167 --> 00:18:04,600
What do you want to drink?

383
00:18:04,700 --> 00:18:06,233
I'll have an oolong tea.

384
00:18:06,333 --> 00:18:07,733
- One oolong tea.
- Coming right up.

385
00:18:08,033 --> 00:18:09,200
What about food?

386
00:18:09,633 --> 00:18:11,767
Just drinks for now.

387
00:18:11,867 --> 00:18:12,900
Yeah.

388
00:18:15,433 --> 00:18:17,167
Mmm, delicious.

389
00:18:17,267 --> 00:18:18,400
Let's toast then.

390
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:19,567
Cheers.

391
00:18:25,333 --> 00:18:26,900
Ah~.

392
00:18:29,100 --> 00:18:30,933
Well, I said I was coming to see Shiono.

393
00:18:31,033 --> 00:18:32,967
And Omaeda said he wanted to tag along.

394
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:36,267
I asked Takoi out for a drink.

395
00:18:36,367 --> 00:18:38,767
Heard he was meeting up with Shiono.

396
00:18:40,600 --> 00:18:43,200
So I wanted to take this
chance to properly apologize.

397
00:18:45,133 --> 00:18:47,500
Didn't you guys have a
huge falling out last time?

398
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:49,833
"Take off your badge
and go home right now."

399
00:18:50,267 --> 00:18:52,567
I just figured it'd be
better if you guys made up.

400
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:55,200
There's nothing to make up for.

401
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:57,133
It was just about work.

402
00:18:58,233 --> 00:18:59,633
I didn't take it to heart at all.

403
00:19:03,500 --> 00:19:05,733
I'm glad to hear him say that.

404
00:19:05,833 --> 00:19:09,867
Omaeda can hold his liquor,
but he's a riot when he's drunk.

405
00:19:10,300 --> 00:19:11,933
Not at all.

406
00:19:12,767 --> 00:19:15,200
Egawa was way funnier last time.

407
00:19:15,300 --> 00:19:16,033
Yeah, totally.

408
00:19:16,133 --> 00:19:21,300
Last time, Egawa got
into it with a regular here.

409
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:23,633
I thought they were going to throw down.

410
00:19:23,733 --> 00:19:26,173
But they ended up drinking
with their arms around each other.

411
00:19:28,433 --> 00:19:29,633
Takoi.

412
00:19:30,267 --> 00:19:31,343
You've got something on your face.

413
00:19:31,367 --> 00:19:33,300
Sorry.

414
00:19:34,100 --> 00:19:35,500
- Thanks.
- There, it's off.

415
00:19:35,967 --> 00:19:37,567
That was seriously hilarious.

416
00:19:46,067 --> 00:19:47,067
What's wrong?

417
00:19:47,700 --> 00:19:48,900
Nothing.

418
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:50,667
It's nothing.

419
00:19:52,133 --> 00:19:53,333
Really?

420
00:19:53,900 --> 00:19:58,033
By the way, my birthday is coming up.

421
00:19:58,133 --> 00:19:59,333
Oh, really?

422
00:19:59,433 --> 00:20:00,200
Yeah.

423
00:20:00,300 --> 00:20:03,067
It's my first birthday since I moved here.

424
00:20:03,167 --> 00:20:04,567
You should get me something.

425
00:20:04,900 --> 00:20:05,700
Ah.

426
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:08,633
Sure, but nothing too expensive.

427
00:20:11,700 --> 00:20:14,033
Then give me this.

428
00:20:14,467 --> 00:20:15,700
This?

429
00:20:15,800 --> 00:20:18,567
I've always thought this one looked cool.

430
00:20:18,667 --> 00:20:19,800
You just want this?

431
00:20:19,900 --> 00:20:21,067
But I've worn it.

432
00:20:21,167 --> 00:20:22,733
That's exactly why I want it.

433
00:20:22,833 --> 00:20:26,833
I was planning to get a new one
anyway, and it wasn't that expensive.

434
00:20:26,933 --> 00:20:27,967
It's yours.

435
00:20:28,067 --> 00:20:29,300
- Really?
- Yeah.

436
00:20:29,667 --> 00:20:30,333
Thanks.

437
00:20:30,433 --> 00:20:31,833
Absolutely not!

438
00:20:40,700 --> 00:20:41,700
I'm leaving.

439
00:20:41,733 --> 00:20:42,433
Wait a minute.

440
00:20:42,533 --> 00:20:43,533
Huh?

441
00:20:43,567 --> 00:20:45,200
Hey, Shiono!

442
00:20:51,267 --> 00:20:52,667
Hey, Shiono!

443
00:20:53,033 --> 00:20:54,333
Hey!

444
00:20:54,933 --> 00:20:56,800
Shiono, wait up!

445
00:20:58,467 --> 00:21:02,467
It wasn't even that expensive.
What's the big deal if I give it to him?

446
00:21:03,233 --> 00:21:05,033
How can you be so oblivious?

447
00:21:05,333 --> 00:21:06,567
Huh?

448
00:21:06,667 --> 00:21:08,700
That guy is hitting on you.

449
00:21:10,433 --> 00:21:11,700
What?

450
00:21:12,467 --> 00:21:14,067
Omaeda?

451
00:21:14,733 --> 00:21:16,067
No way.

452
00:21:18,767 --> 00:21:21,133
Weren't we supposed to just
meet up, the two of us, today?

453
00:21:22,600 --> 00:21:26,600
That's because he said
he wanted to apologize for last time.

454
00:21:26,700 --> 00:21:28,833
It's because you keep
giving him the time of day.

455
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:30,300
Huh?

456
00:21:31,333 --> 00:21:34,167
If this keeps up, he's only
going to push his luck.

457
00:21:34,900 --> 00:21:35,900
Hold on.

458
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:41,267
Even if that were true, it's
not like I'd cheat on you.

459
00:21:43,633 --> 00:21:44,800
I know.

460
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:48,633
You're just too nice, and
you're nice to everyone.

461
00:21:49,433 --> 00:21:51,900
You can't just turn away
people who like you.

462
00:21:52,933 --> 00:21:54,033
What?

463
00:21:54,133 --> 00:21:56,233
Even if you don't like them that much,

464
00:21:56,833 --> 00:22:00,233
if they make a move, you'd just
go along with it, wouldn't you?

465
00:22:02,700 --> 00:22:04,400
Is that really what you think?

466
00:22:08,233 --> 00:22:13,200
I always thought you understood how I felt.

467
00:22:17,367 --> 00:22:18,267
I'm sorry.

468
00:22:18,367 --> 00:22:19,633
I'm leaving.

469
00:22:21,467 --> 00:22:22,467
Hey!

470
00:22:23,333 --> 00:22:24,833
You're being so unreasonable!

471
00:22:24,867 --> 00:22:27,500
(This drama is purely fictional.)

472
00:22:27,933 --> 00:22:29,267
(Finale)

473
00:22:29,333 --> 00:22:30,633
(Finale Preview)
I like Takoi.

474
00:22:30,733 --> 00:22:32,867
Want to just keep things casual with me?

475
00:22:33,467 --> 00:22:34,467
Where's Takoi?

476
00:22:34,533 --> 00:22:37,367
I heard someone who looks like Omaeda
is roaming around downtown.

477
00:22:37,467 --> 00:22:39,367
Since you're already here,

478
00:22:39,467 --> 00:22:40,233
let's have some fun.

479
00:22:40,333 --> 00:22:43,000
Takoi.

480
00:22:43,800 --> 00:22:44,933
Freeze!

481
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:46,133
Damn it!
